Vice President

US Financial Consulting Group - Based in Toronto

Richter Consulting, Inc. (“RCI”) is a member of the Richter Group, a full-service business advisory firm, founded in 1926. RCI serves its clients with a multidisciplinary group of 6 partners and ~25 professionals. We work with US-based leverage lenders and private equity firms regarding their portfolio companies/investments. Our clients call upon our experienced professionals to provide our expertise in Business Assessment, Cashflow Forecasting, Financial Reorganization/Profitability Improvement, Crisis Management, Transaction Advisory and Asset-Based Lending Diligence, among other services.
A Career with a High Rate of Return:

What’s in it for you?

Experience in a specialized, highly regarded consulting practice;
Exposure to sophisticated US-based corporations;
A unique learning experience in financial modeling, incorporating cash flow/liquidity;
Insight into operational strategies, revenue drivers, profitability improvement, cost savings, KPI analysis, etc.;
Draw upon your accounting/finance fundamentals and apply them to real-life situations;
Participate in diverse engagements, exposure to a variety of companies, industries, competitive landscapes, etc.;
Become well-rounded, developing soft and technical skills;
Work directly with experienced Partners;
Limited travel in the USA;
Join a team willing and committed to investing in your development.

Position overview:

Work within a multidisciplinary team of ~30 professionals on a variety of stimulating engagements (typically 6 weeks). Our deal teams of 3-4 professionals deliver consulting services involving companies in numerous industries (Consumer Products, Pharma, Distribution, Services, Manufacturing, etc.) experiencing challenges arising from over-leverage, liquidity problems, under-performance, macroeconomic events, or other business transitional/operating issues.

Our clients’ portfolio companies typically include privately-owned small-medium sized businesses ($100MM-$500MM in revenue), which offers the opportunity to work along-side company executives and upper management to identify and recommend solutions to complex business issues.
A variety of arrangements are available including a hybrid work schedule.
What we are looking for:

Minimum 6 years of relevant experience;
Diligence and transaction advisory service an asset; 
Proficient in Excel and PowerPoint (Alteryx or Power Query/Pivot a plus);
Strong aptitude for quantitative and qualitative analyses;
Willingness to learn and adapt in a changing environment;
Ability to collaborate with client personnel and other professionals;
Excellent communication (written and verbal), presentation, and organizational skills;
A positive and energetic attitude;
Ability to work autonomously.

